  "notes": "ORGAN pathfinding run sets a 90% CL limit g_agamma > 2.02e-12 GeV^-1 at 26.531 GHz (110 ueV) over a narrow 2.5 neV span. The text-quoted '2.02e-12 eV^-1' is a typo; the exclusion plot y-axis is in GeV^-1. Local DM density of 0.45 GeV/cm^3 is stated for projections; same is assumed for the pathfinder. Single limit point extracted as the result is a very narrow Lorentzian-shaped span around 110 ueV. | Vision: Figure 3 (image 7) shows the ORGAN Pathfinder exclusion as a very narrow vertical bar near 110 ueV (26.531 GHz). The exclusion is a single narrow Lorentzian-shaped feature spanning only ~2.5 neV, not a continuous boundary across the plotted mass range. The bar extends downward from CAST line (~6.6e-11) to a tip near g_agamma ~2.0e-12, matching the abstract stated limit of 2.02e-12 eV^-1 (note: abstract gives 2.02e-12 eV^-1; in GeV^-1 this corresponds to ~2.02e-12 as read from the vertical bar tip). The orange lines are CAST limits and KSVZ/DFSZ bands; the blue line is the QCD axion line. Data points represent the single narrow exclusion feature, not a swept boundary. | CV axis calibration succeeded (ranges consistent with LLM) | Curve traced by classical CV | Calibration: No calibration needed (benchmark KSVZ raw_ratio=1.03 snapped to identity)",
